14:(see Q0).
20:| Q0 | **The brief and `stories.md` disagree** on group children loading. The brief puts "a group loading its children (view-computed state, `WantsBlink`)" in criterion 1. `stories.md` §A-10a criterion 1 says "source: the registry, **without `WantsBlink`**" and lists children loading as out of scope; `inventory.md` gap 3 (validated 2026-11-06) explains why: `TreeNode.Loading` is never drawn on a row — `→` makes the group the current level at once (`navigation.go:26`), so the group is no longer a visible row while its children load; the load is the global footer line `Loading GitLab groups...` (`view.go:139`). The only reachable case is `←` pressed before the answer lands, where the global footer spinner is still on. | **A** follow `stories.md`: registry only (create, delete), no `WantsBlink`, children loading stays the footer spinner · **B** add `WantsBlink()` + a view-computed `Running` for a visible group row with `Loading == true` (only reachable after `←` during a load), plus a footer sentence for it (none is validated in `ux.md` §1.2) | **A**: there is no per-node spinner to remove; B adds a state for a corner case already covered by the footer, and an unvalidated footer phrase. The plan below assumes A. |
21:| Q1 | **A failed create has no row.** `handleGroupCreated` / `handleProjectCreated` drop the placeholder on failure (`settleCreating(target, nil)`), so criterion 3 ("select the line, the footer gives the cause") cannot hold for a create as the code stands. The remembered failure is keyed on the *predicted* path, and nothing refuses a name that already exists, so that key can be the path of a healthy existing row. | **A** keep a failed placeholder row showing `⊗` until the next create with the same name, `ctrl+r` or a view rebuild; effort M (a node flag the registry does not know, so a rebuilt view loses the row while the registry keeps the failure; dedupe on retry; every action refused on it) · **B** as today, row dropped; read `create` failures on every row → a failure on an existing name paints a healthy row `⊗ last create failed` that no create can clear · **C** as today, row dropped; read the `create` kind only on placeholder rows (`node.Creating`), so a create failure is the 3 s `Error` (`Failed to create g/app — <cause>`) plus the failed run in `:jobs`, and never a `⊗`. Delete failures get the full criterion 3. | **C**: keeps the story at S, never marks a healthy row, and the legend's "stays until the next attempt on that row" stays true. A is a UX change of its own (a row that outlives its request). Criterion 3 is then met for delete and, for create, by the event and `:jobs` only. |
